WEBVTT

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:01.810
I am happy.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:07.440
My blood protected you... My son.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.490
Wait!

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.370
I finally... I finally met you!

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.870
L-Leol!

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:24.890
The King of Monaco... is dead.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.760
But... I...

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.500
I can no longer meet Father!

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:32.720
It’s not like you can no longer meet him.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:33.680
Huh?

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.100
I’ll help you meet him.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:35.970
Huh?

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.270
Oh yeah!

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:42.310
<i>Japan</i> #44 might be able to
take Pierrot to heaven once again!

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.020
No, that’s impossible.

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:44.520
Huh?

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.440
Well, I don’t have the petalite I need to make #44.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.450
Then, what’ll you do?

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:50.900
That’s easy.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:55.000
All I have to do is make an even more amazing bread!

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:00.420
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:02.380
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:04.630
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.970
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:13.180
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.060
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:50.730
I’ll show you the universe!!

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:52.910
The man who’ll inherit the <i>Gopan</i>!

00:02:54.860 --> 00:03:00.160
Either way, in order to win against Shadow’s <i>Gopan</i>, I need a really outstanding bread.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.600
If it’s not a bread good enough to send Pierrot to the other side for certain,

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.240
then we have no chance of winning.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.790
C... Can you really make that amazing a bread?!

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.920
Of course I can.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.250
But...

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:15.670
Hey, will you be able to help me
collect any ingredient that I want?

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.550
P-Probably.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:19.880
But, what in the world are you trying to make?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.470
A new type of <i>Japan</i>.

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:24.260
<i>Japan</i> #61.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.470
And it’s called... Cannabis <i>Japan</i>!

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:27.480
Cannabis <i>Japan</i>?!

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:31.690
C... Cannabis <i>Japan</i>?

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.190
You want to make a <i>Japan</i> with cannabis?!

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.020
Yeah.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.940
Quit kidding around, will you!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.230
About what?

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:41.820
“About what,” this stupid fellow asks...

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.370
There’s no way that you’d be allowed to make bread for a competition

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:45.990
with something illegal like that.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:48.410
I-Illegal?

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.120
What are you talking about?!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:53.120
Cannabis is in things like the
shichimi spice mix we use all the time.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.090
I should be the one asking you
what you’re talking about!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:56.920
Look.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.140
It’s not just me. They’re surprised, too.

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:02.840
Uh... They’re not surprised.

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:06.100
Hey! Weren’t you surprised until a moment ago?!

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:10.180
I was just surprised about
whether it would go well with bread.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:14.230
It’s common sense that it’s in shichimi.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:17.190
And I just showed surprise because I’m a clown.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.150
W-Wait.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:22.740
Even children know that cannabis is illegal.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.910
Then, why’s it included in shichimi?

00:04:25.370 --> 00:04:27.080
Because the seeds are legal.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.330
Huh?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.290
It’s legal to import seeds that have been processed so that they don’t sprout.

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:37.340
And it’s legal to cultivate them for foodstuff if you have the proper license, even in Japan.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:38.880
That’s right.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.180
My grandpa’s friend has a proper license to cultivate it at their farm.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.430
It’s perfectly good business.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.090
A-Are you guys for real?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:48.810
Yep, it’s true.

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.100
In addition to being used in shichimi,
hemp seeds are used in soba.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:55.060
Didn’t you know that in Shimokitazawa, Tokyo, there is a restaurant called “Asa,”

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.230
which specializes in dishes containing cannabis?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.610
No, I didn’t know that...

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.490
Well, leaving aside Kawachi, who completely lacks common sense,

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:08.370
let’s go to the Royal Palace since we have
plenty there and you can use all you like.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.080
Yahoo!

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.580
What kind of palace is this?

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:12.790
But...

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.790
You must really make a bread
delicious enough to send me to heaven.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:19.540
Yep!

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.550
Leave it to me!

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:27.050
Man, that surprised me.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.890
To think that cannabis seeds were
present in the shichimi spice mix...

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:34.940
Yeah, I was surprised on hearing about it, too.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:35.770
Right?

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.360
If it were a regular person,
then it’s understandable...

00:05:38.360 --> 00:05:41.400
But, to think there’s trash among chefs who don’t even know that much...

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.360
You said it.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.110
In general, there are too many
people who have misconceptions about it.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:52.700
Cannabis, also known as hemp, is a food item that has been around since the Joumon era.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:56.210
If the wrong ideas about its use
hadn’t come from across the sea,

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:59.710
there would still be large fields of cannabis in Japan.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:01.800
Listen up, Kawachi.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.930
In addition to containing the
essential amino acids an adult needs daily,

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.390
a handful of hemp seeds can help
strengthen the immunity of the body.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.390
Also, it has an exceptional
flavor that entrances all who try it.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.270
I-I see...

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:19.230
Hemp seeds are awesome.

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.320
With this, it’ll be an easy win
against Shadow, right Azuma?

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:24.150
Yep!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.200
I’ll do my best!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.950
No, we can’t relax yet.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:34.000
Shadow is a terrifying man,
greatly exceeding our expectations.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.580
Terrifying man?

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:43.340
Actually, when you guys were at the Royal Palace, my friend Kid got in touch with me.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.960
Hey, Ryou.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.670
Oh, Kid!

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:50.050
I’ve finally gotten my hands on
the information you were waiting for.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.600
I’ve discovered the truth about that Shadow guy.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.470
What?!

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:55.600
So, who the hell is he?!

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.810
Don’t be too surprised.

00:06:57.810 --> 00:06:59.890
That Shadow guy is...

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.350
a pantomimer!

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.190
A pantomimer?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:06.520
And, he’s supposedly as good as the
world-renowned genius pantomimer,

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.780
Marcel Marceau!

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:10.610
That’s how good he’s supposed to be.

00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.790
As good as Marcel Marceau?!

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.870
Marcel Marceau.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.830
The greatest pantomimer on Earth.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:22.580
A genius who mimed everything,
including aging, life and death.

00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:28.840
Shadow is an equal to the
godlike Marcel Marceau, you say?

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.090
Hey you.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:31.180
You ass.

00:07:31.180 --> 00:07:32.470
You dropped me again.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:33.430
Hey, Ryou.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.550
Pick up the receiver.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:35.600
You ass.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.850
And that’s what the situation seems to be.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.440
You’re not a bad kidder either, Kuro-yan.

00:07:41.440 --> 00:07:42.190
What do you mean?

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.940
So, I understand that Shadow
is an outstanding pantomimer.

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:51.200
Azuma’s going to be challenging him
only on the “pan” and not the pantomime.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.700
So, there’s no way that Azuma could lose...

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.910
This is why bald, ignorant trash like you are annoying.

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:56.830
Again?

00:07:57.530 --> 00:08:02.040
I’m sure you’ve seen circus and pantomime
performances which imitated something, right?

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.580
That kind of performance can only
be achieved by people with great talent

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.210
who have gone through a great deal of hard work.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:12.550
In the end, they are able to imitate any movement, no matter how complex.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.640
I-I see!

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:18.970
That’s why Kinoshita, who’s from a circus,
is good at imitating other people’s breads.

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.850
Kinoshita?

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.310
I’ve never heard of that character...

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.360
Still, no matter how good he is at copying,

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.570
his bread won’t be any good unless he
has an extremely good person to copy from.

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:33.150
If he copies Shachihoko or Monica,

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:36.160
he’ll be copying someone very good, but...

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.580
I don’t think that he’s all that
dangerous an opponent for Azuma.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.290
What are you talking about?!

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.040
That’s not the level he’ll be copying from.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.670
He’s got the ultimate person to copy from.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.170
Huh?

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.050
The creator of the <i>Gopan</i> and the greatest baker in the world...

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:53.180
The owner of St. Pierre, Kirisaki Yuuichi!

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:54.430
Kirisaki...

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.630
Yuuichi?

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.070
Not yet.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.280
You’ve only managed to copy it to 98%.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.790
Come on, stand.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.200
And copy me.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:25.540
100% of me.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.340
Please don’t be unreasonable.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:41.810
I have copied your superhuman bread
kneading to 98% in this short period of time.

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:46.310
If I’m to push myself any more
than this, my body will break.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.190
#1 in the world.

00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.270
If you don’t wish to be #1 in
the world, you can just stop.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.790
I...

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:11.210
As far back as I can remember,
I knew that I had a special talent.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.290
That was...

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:15.170
Oh, it’s exactly the same!

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:18.010
It’s Barry Bonds’ pose after he hits a home run.

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:20.300
And that was the fact that I could imitate other people.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.850
That’s amazing form, Shadow.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.060
That’s the world’s #1 swing.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:31.520
Thanks to this talent, I could
imitate any sportsman’s form easily.

00:10:31.980 --> 00:10:36.360
If I can copy the form of the #1
people in the world, I can be #1 in the world.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.570
I can be the most skillful person in the world.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:40.530
But...

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.570
Strike!

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:43.530
Batter out!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.700
Game set.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:49.750
Geez. Even if your form is exactly like his, it doesn’t mean anything if you can’t hit the ball.

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.420
I guess in the end he’s just imitating blindly.

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.900
Our loss today is your fault.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:58.670
Being introverted by nature, I
never had any friends to begin with.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.090
After that, no one would talk to me.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:03.840
That’s why I looked...

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.350
for something that I could become #1 in the world at

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:11.060
by relying only on my ability to copy, and not on things like speed and muscular strength.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:13.100
That’s right!

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:15.560
That something was pantomime.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:19.570
If it’s pantomime, even I can be #1 in the world.

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:24.070
After that, I stopped going to
school and just watched videos.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:30.080
At that time, I found videos of Marcel Marceau,

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.420
I copied his movements perfectly.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:38.420
And, after a few years, I had
his movements down perfectly.

00:11:38.420 --> 00:11:39.340
But...

00:11:39.840 --> 00:11:41.300
Shadow!

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.930
How long do you plan on locking yourself up in here?!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:46.140
If you don’t cut it out,
I’m going to throw you out!

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.480
If you don’t cut it out,
I’m going to throw you out!

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:57.440
Wh-What’s with you?!

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.820
I’m sorry, Mommy.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.570
I was just joking.

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:04.550
I’d been imitating people for so very long that

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:08.280
unless I rolled my eyes so I couldn’t see them,

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:12.080
I’d reflexively imitate everything they said or did.

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:15.080
There was no turning back.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.220
My imitations are perfect.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:28.890
But...

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:33.560
Even with my skill at pantomime,
my glory days didn’t last long.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:36.730
You won’t make a contract with me?!

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:38.270
Why not, Mr. President?!

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:39.570
I’ll tell you straight.

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:43.820
It’s because your mime has no soul.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:48.830
Without soul, your mime cannot truly become art.

00:12:51.280 --> 00:12:53.540
Don’t mess with me!

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:54.850
Soul, you say?!

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.660
Art, you say?!

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:58.840
Don’t make fun of me!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.800
After the contract for the production was scrapped,

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.470
I wandered the roads, wasting away.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:11.050
I... I’m #1 in the world.

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:12.720
It was then...

00:13:12.720 --> 00:13:14.940
that I met him.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:19.270
You want to be #1 in the world?

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.690
Shadow White-kun?

00:13:22.190 --> 00:13:24.700
That man called himself Kirisaki.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:29.240
You want a pantomimer like me to
participate in a bread tournament?

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.700
Yeah. There is a #1 spot in
the world over there as well.

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.990
Quit joking around.

00:13:33.990 --> 00:13:36.580
Far from making bread, I
can’t even make a decent meal...

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:38.160
Copy me.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:40.330
All you have to do is copy me.

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.590
I’m the #1 baker in the world after all.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.120
In the world of food,

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.600
as long as one follows a recipe, anyone can make the same thing to a certain extent.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:54.850
And, fortunately, it’s not like I
possess special hands or anything.

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.600
Since you’re capable of copying people perfectly,

00:13:57.600 --> 00:14:02.150
it’s quite possible that you can become #1 in the world.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:04.610
#1 in the world?

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.730
That’s right.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.110
#1 in the world.

00:14:07.440 --> 00:14:09.610
#1 in the world?

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.540
I’d be #1 in the world?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.870
Very well, Mr. Kirisaki.

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:22.840
I’ll copy you perfectly... 100%.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:27.090
But, there’s only one thing that I’d like to ask you.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:27.880
What is it?

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:35.760
As to whether it’s really necessary
to go so far against that Azuma guy.

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:40.400
When I look at him, all I’m left with
is the impression of a regular idiot.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:43.270
Don’t underestimate idiots, Shadow-kun!

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.820
Van Gogh, who cut off his own ear.

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.170
Dali, who supposedly ate a live spider.

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:51.280
Edison, who failed elementary school.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.110
Those people who are called geniuses now

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:57.620
have all done things that can’t
be called anything but idiotic.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:02.500
This is the reason that they say, “There’s a fine line between the genius and the fool.”

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:07.380
It is proof that being an idiot allows
you to concentrate on a single thing.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:13.800
The reason that Shachihoko lost was due to the
concentration of that idiotic fellow from Kansai.

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:18.770
In the first place, the reason that you were able
to copy Marcel Marceau’s performance perfectly

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:23.270
was that you were able to concentrate insanely.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:25.560
Listen up, Shadow-kun.

00:15:25.560 --> 00:15:28.370
Just like the time you were
able to copy Marcel perfectly...

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.480
become an idiot once again.

00:15:30.480 --> 00:15:36.290
And earnestly imitate my ultimate masterpiece, <i>Gopan</i>!

00:15:37.780 --> 00:15:43.000
If you do that, you should be able to show the judge, Pierrot, the universe!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.210
Th-The universe?!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:50.840
That’s right.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.590
This is a rumor, but...

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:56.010
It seems that people who have eaten the <i>Gopan</i> made personally by him...

00:15:56.010 --> 00:16:00.050
feel like they are floating in the Milky Way.

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.230
A taste that makes you feel like
you’re floating in the Milky Way?!

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:06.980
But, Azuma has sent you to heaven, right?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.020
I don’t quite get it, but...

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.730
If it’s a match between heaven
and the universe, won’t heaven win?

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:11.850
I wonder...

00:16:12.730 --> 00:16:14.700
At that time, even Azuma said it.

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:20.710
With <i>Japan</i> #44, the reason I was able
to go to heaven was that I’m sensitive.

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.370
But...

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:28.120
That <i>Gopan</i> seems to also be able to take
regular people to the ends of the universe.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:30.210
Wh-What was that?!

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:34.920
So, if sensitive people like me or Pierrot are to eat it,

00:16:34.920 --> 00:16:38.520
we might even be transported
beyond the universe or something!

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.260
So, prepare yourself, Azuma!

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:45.570
While the enemy is Shadow, it’s not Shadow!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.850
Greater than anyone else in the world,

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:51.270
it’s the #1 baker in the world, Kirisaki Yuuichi.

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:54.110
If you don’t meet him with the best
<i>Japan</i> ever, you can’t possibly win!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.990
All right!

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:10.960
It’s the finals tomorrow morning.

00:17:10.960 --> 00:17:13.000
I wonder if Azuma is all right...?

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:14.170
I wonder...

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.220
What do you mean, you wonder...?

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:17.220
Either way...

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:21.630
We just need to figure out where to run if Azuma loses.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:25.940
If you have a place in mind, please let me know.

00:17:26.350 --> 00:17:29.100
I’d like to see the pandas in China.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.940
I want to see the Moai statues on Easter Island.

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:36.360
Well, I’d like to see the Sagrada Familia in Spain...

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:37.860
Stop kidding around!

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.700
Why are you thinking of losing before even trying?!

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:45.000
I mean, if he loses, we’ll be so broke
we won’t even be able to board a plane!

00:17:45.450 --> 00:17:47.040
Oh, that’s true I guess...

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.830
First, we’d have to figure out
a new way to borrow money.

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:51.960
I’ll leave that to you.

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:52.960
Okay!

00:17:55.540 --> 00:17:56.590
Geez.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.170
There’s no point in talking to them.

00:17:58.170 --> 00:17:59.880
What’s wrong with them?

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.380
Kawachi-san.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:01.970
What is it?

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:03.850
It’s all right.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:09.430
Actually, I asked Manager the
same question in the afternoon.

00:18:09.430 --> 00:18:10.930
And...

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:15.190
Tsukino, what’s the most
important thing when you make bread?

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:15.610
Huh?

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:17.820
Umm...

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:21.240
If it were me, I’d take the
person who eats it into consideration.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.530
Yeah. That’s it.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.120
Not too sweet.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.600
Not too salty.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.120
Not too hard.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:29.750
Not too soft.

00:18:30.120 --> 00:18:33.370
The most important thing for us is to bake bread

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:36.330
by thinking about the people who’ll eat it.

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:37.420
But!

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:41.270
What does that have to do
with not advising Azuma-san?

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.500
Right now,

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.930
Azuma is earnestly baking bread just to help that Pierrot guy meet his parents again.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:50.770
Artisans with such feelings
are stronger than anyone else.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.430
He won’t lose!

00:18:52.430 --> 00:18:53.980
B-But...

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:59.030
If we were to offer any advice,
all we’d do is confuse him.

00:19:00.190 --> 00:19:03.360
If you doubt me, then peek in
and take a look at his eyes.

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:04.750
O-Okay.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:11.750
Th-This is...

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:18.260
Azuma-san!

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.760
And, that’s how it is.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:25.680
Despite what he says, Manager always looks carefully and understands the situation.

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.770
Is that so?

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:30.870
So, for now we should just believe in Azuma-san

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:33.780
and only concern ourselves with cheering for him tomorrow.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:36.190
Okay. I understand.

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:40.780
What do you mean, concern ourselves
with cheering for him tomorrow?

00:19:46.570 --> 00:19:50.450
What’s with this amazing number of people?!

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:53.420
Could it be... that this is what you meant with
concerning ourselves with cheering for him?!

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:55.750
Yes! That’s right!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:20:00.420
After all, Pierrot-san is really popular
all over the world as the Miracle Prince.

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:06.390
There’s a lot of regular tourists who
came here to catch a glimpse of Pierrot-san.

00:20:06.590 --> 00:20:08.760
I’ll be late again at this rate.

00:20:08.760 --> 00:20:10.010
Don’t worry.

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:11.430
I’ve made preparations.

00:20:11.430 --> 00:20:12.350
Look!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.650
A-A helicopter has come to get us?!

00:20:21.520 --> 00:20:23.900
All people concerned...

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:26.320
Please climb this ladder and come on up.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:29.120
Can’t you come get us in a more regular manner?!

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.660
I don’t wanna!

00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:38.460
Shut up and climb quickly!

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:45.720
Well, it seems like I’m more
popular than I’d have imagined...

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:47.970
I’m pretty surprised myself.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:50.470
Let... Let me down!

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:51.680
Geez.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:55.430
How pathetic to be afraid of heights
when you’re supposed to be a warrior.

00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:56.480
Compared to that...

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:01.990
Even though he’s going to be fighting
a Kirisaki clone soon, he’s quite calm.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:06.360
I guess artisans who are
earnestly making something for someone

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.490
don’t care about their opponents.

00:21:10.280 --> 00:21:11.910
His opponent is strong, but...

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.570
Azuma is a genius himself!

00:21:13.570 --> 00:21:15.960
As long as he holds onto
those feelings, he’ll be sure to win.

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.660
Oh, I’m sorry.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:21.210
Sorry for the trouble caused to you because of me.

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.800
Old Ma... I mean Mister Pierrot...

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:27.500
I’ll be sure to transport you to heaven.

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:29.550
So, be sure to meet your father once again.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:35.440
Yeah.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:36.560
You’re right.

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:38.220
Hey there.

00:21:38.220 --> 00:21:39.970
The tears are here too soon.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:42.980
Keep them for when you meet your father.

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.480
I know that.

00:21:44.480 --> 00:21:46.570
I know that, but I’m really happy.

00:21:47.400 --> 00:21:50.690
When I think that I’ll be able to
meet both my mother and father...

00:21:50.690 --> 00:21:52.830
I can’t keep my happiness in check.

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.780
I guess that’s true...

00:21:54.780 --> 00:21:57.700
If you’re to meet both your mother and father...

00:21:57.700 --> 00:21:58.950
Mother?!

00:21:58.950 --> 00:22:00.080
That’s right!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:03.870
Azuma’s opponent, Shadow White, has promised to send me to the other end of the universe,

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:10.840
where I’ll be able to meet my
mother who’s become a star.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:12.090
What was that?!

00:22:12.090 --> 00:22:13.300
Shadow did?!

00:22:13.300 --> 00:22:14.930
And with your mother, too?!

00:22:30.870 --> 00:22:32.700
I challenge you!

00:24:05.340 --> 00:24:09.130
With the title of #1 in the world on the line,
we’d like you to make the ultimate bread!

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.970
The opponent is the strongest he’s faced since the start of the program, Shadow White!

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:14.190
Looks like it will be a spectacular battle.

00:24:14.190 --> 00:24:15.650
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan,

00:24:15.650 --> 00:24:17.350
All the ultimate ingredients collected!!

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:19.020
The greatest finals in all of history!

00:24:19.020 --> 00:24:19.900
Be sure to watch.

00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:22.650
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:22.900 --> 00:24:26.020
Pantomime is a form of acting
where you don’t use words or props.

00:24:26.020 --> 00:24:27.820
You can perform it anywhere.

00:24:27.820 --> 00:24:31.630
And even foreigners who don’t understand the language can understand it, ’kay?

00:24:32.070 --> 00:24:33.870
Oh, okay!
